  "limitations": [
    "Three synthetic task families test operand-combination transfer across split-exclusive prompt templates, not broad reasoning or cybersecurity competence.",
    "Each split contains only 18 or 36 examples; estimates are descriptive and are not powered generalization claims.",
    "The test split is in the public repository and is not secret; runtime access logging does not prevent a human from reading it.",
    "No cross-split pair exceeds the fixed 0.82 character-trigram similarity threshold; semantic similarity can still escape this surface metric.",
    "Character-trigram similarity misses semantic leakage; the task index is needed to detect input-combination overlap.",
    "The tokenizer is fit only on the train split, but shared task vocabulary across splits is intentional and does not imply independent lexical domains.",
    "10 answer starts fall inside a BPE token; answer-bearing loss includes the intersecting token and is not strict answer-only loss for those rows.",
    "A separate human quality review remains required before experiment admission."
